WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.360
It has long been the mission of the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation to secure and contain any anomalies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:11.280
they encounter, all to protect the safety of&nbsp;
the human race. Sometimes, containing an SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.960
is a trivial task, as simple as guarding a room&nbsp;
or keeping an eye on an artifact with strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.920
but mostly harmless, properties. Other times&nbsp;
though, anomalies require a considerable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.640
number of the Foundation’s personnel and&nbsp;
resources to keep them under control.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.440
This latter category commonly includes some of&nbsp;
the more dangerous creatures and entities that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:37.280
the SCP Foundation keeps under lock and key.
However, while it might be only in very rare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:43.520
cases, every so often an SCP comes along with&nbsp;
its very own built-in method of containment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.600
This can often be the result of someone&nbsp;
encountering an anomaly and discovering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.600
the perfect way of imprisoning it before the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation comes along and steals all the credit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.200
Undoubtedly, this makes the job of securing an&nbsp;
anomaly all the easier for the Foundation’s staff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:04.480
After all, someone else has already done the hard&nbsp;
part of that job for them. Or rather, it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:10.080
make things easier, if only the Foundation’s&nbsp;
own researchers chose not to interfere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.760
and could leave a deadly threat kept safely in its&nbsp;
box without trying to find out what makes it tick.&nbsp;

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:22.880
SCP-5001 is, in some ways, a reminder that some&nbsp;
things are best left alone. But it is also a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.640
grave warning not to tamper with that which&nbsp;
you do not understand. Both of these lessons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:34.640
would soon be imparted on the SCP Foundation.
Buried sixty kilometers below the ground in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:41.840
Northern Russia is SCP-5001, a fifty three&nbsp;
kilometer wide structure. It is an enormous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:47.440
biomechanical machine, but to the untrained eye,&nbsp;
there is nothing anomalous about the object.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:53.120
And according to the Foundation’s findings, this&nbsp;
is indeed the case, there is nothing inherently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.840
anomalous about the structure itself.
But there are a number of characteristics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:03.040
that seem to suggest it is, in some way,&nbsp;
connected to anomalous phenomena. For one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.840
there’s the sheer scale of the structure. And&nbsp;
then there’s the records that were uncovered about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:13.440
SCP-5001, which appear to have been&nbsp;
monitoring and tracking its status.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:18.880
Perhaps whoever constructed it, or discovered&nbsp;
it, kept a record as they observed the structure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:21.840
Nothing too out of the ordinary&nbsp;
about that, but what’s strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:30.080
is that these date back to 11,000 BC, and yet were&nbsp;
somehow made with modern systems of measurement.&nbsp;

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:35.360
And other, weirder documents have been&nbsp;
recovered from inside of SCP-5001,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:41.200
records written in languages from all over the&nbsp;
world, and even some in languages lost to time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:47.040
Among them are papers in Phoenician, Ancient&nbsp;
Hebrew, both Ancient and Modern Greek, Latin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.640
Anglo-Saxon, along with Modern Russian, English,&nbsp;
and Mandarin. Some of these documents are even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.320
written in languages that the SCP Foundation’s&nbsp;
top researchers are yet to properly identify.&nbsp;

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:02.800
The explanation for all this would seem&nbsp;
obvious, wouldn’t it? Writing in both ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:08.320
and contemporary languages, records that date all&nbsp;
the way back to the last of the prehistoric era.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:15.920
It all seems to point in a certain direction:&nbsp;
Somehow, SCP-5001 has a link to time travel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.440
Perhaps it was even a hub for a&nbsp;
group of time travelers, right?&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.880
Wrong.
The Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:26.080
already thought that might be the case, and&nbsp;
checked for any signs of temporal anomalies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:31.840
And yet, they found nothing, no evidence to&nbsp;
suggest that there had even been any time travel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:39.840
near or using SCP-5001. There were no devices on&nbsp;
site that could affect time, and no traces of any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:46.960
residue or fallout from a temporal occurrence.
So, what exactly does this thing even do? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.680
we’re afraid to say the Foundation researchers&nbsp;
have been stumped on the answer to that question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:57.760
too, and they are not the only ones, either. Way&nbsp;
back in the fifties, the GRU’s Division P also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:03.120
had an interest in SCP-5001. For anyone&nbsp;
who isn't already acquainted with them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:08.320
they are one of the SCP Foundation’s numerous&nbsp;
Groups of Interest, a list of organizations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:13.920
corporations, and agencies from around the&nbsp;
world who have also had dealings with anomalies.&nbsp;

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:19.520
In the case of GRU-P, they were originally a&nbsp;
division of the Russian army during the Cold War.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:25.040
The specialty of GRU Division P was the&nbsp;
acquisition of anomalous objects and entities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:30.640
In other words, they were the Soviet&nbsp;
Union’s very own SCP Foundation.&nbsp;

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:36.240
In 1953, GRU Division P was alerted to&nbsp;
abnormal seismic activity in a narrow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:40.480
region of Northern Russia. A team was&nbsp;
immediately sent in to investigate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:44.960
and began attempting to take seismological&nbsp;
measurements of the area in question. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:50.880
their various experiments and tests, GRU Division&nbsp;
P realized a discrepancy in their readings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.920
Again and again they checked and double-checked&nbsp;
their results, only to discover that this reading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:02.080
wasn’t the result of faulty equipment or even&nbsp;
human error. There was something big nearby.&nbsp;

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:06.640
What they hadn’t yet realized was that around&nbsp;
thirty kilometers away, deep underground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:14.480
was SCP-5001. Immediately, GRU Division P began&nbsp;
drilling towards the location of SCP-5001,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:19.520
but for years found that they were unable to&nbsp;
breach the exterior of the structure. Defeated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:26.080
the project was abandoned in 1955. However, Soviet&nbsp;
leader First Secretary Khrushchev seemed to have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:33.680
vested interest in gaining access to SCP-5001. As&nbsp;
a result, he privately funded the GRU Division P&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:38.320
operation, allowing them to continue their&nbsp;
work in secret for a number of years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:45.040
from 1959 until Khrushchev was deposed in 1964.
Of course, this was all during the height of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:51.280
Cold War, but by the late 1960s, international&nbsp;
relations between the Soviet Union and the United&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:56.880
States of America were starting to ease. Thanks to&nbsp;
the relaxing tensions, a contract was introduced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:01.680
allowing the two nations’ secret organizations&nbsp;
to work together on a number of operations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:07.200
involving potentially dangerous anomalies.
This meant that the SCP Foundation was finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:14.080
able to step in and contribute to the GRU&nbsp;
Division P’s project concerning SCP-5001.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:19.360
Their first task? Actually getting inside&nbsp;
the subterranean structure. Naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:24.720
given how well versed the Foundation is in dealing&nbsp;
with anomalies, they had ideas for how to crack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:29.920
this nut. By acquiring anomalous technology from&nbsp;
the Global Occult Coalition, another Group of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:36.080
Interest, as well as experimental designs created&nbsp;
by one Doctor Elijah Rachma, the SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:42.480
were finally able to breach the structure in 1971.
From then until the dissolution of the Soviet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:49.040
Union in 1991, the SCP Foundation and GRU Division&nbsp;
P worked together to conduct a number of studies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:56.000
into the origin and purpose of SCP-5001. Both&nbsp;
organizations were curious as to the technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:01.280
the structure possessed, and attempts were even&nbsp;
made to recreate some of the devices found within.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:06.720
Among this advanced technology were Ontological&nbsp;
Stabilizers, also known as Scranton Reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:13.120
Anchors, which are located around SCP-5001’s inner&nbsp;
chamber. These were designed to directly alter the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:16.640
amount of Humes in a given area.
What’s a Hume?&nbsp;

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:22.480
Well, to keep it simple, a Hume is a measure&nbsp;
of the reality around us. If it helps, imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:28.000
reality as a pile of sand. Now imagine that you&nbsp;
remove a single grain of sand from the pile.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:33.440
Congratulations, you just removed one Hume&nbsp;
from this reality. Taking one away doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:39.200
really do much, but start grabbing handfuls&nbsp;
and the pile gets smaller, scattered, less a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:45.120
pile and more a light dusting of sand. Reality&nbsp;
works the same way. Take too much of it away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:50.640
and it starts to lose whatever it was before.
Being able to alter the amount of Humes in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:55.760
area meant that these Ontological Stabilizers&nbsp;
could alter the strength of reality itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:01.200
even nullify the reality bending properties of&nbsp;
some anomalies. In theory, an SCP with the power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:06.400
to influence reality could be contained using this&nbsp;
technology, the effects of their abilities reduced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:11.760
significantly although not negated entirely.
Another noteworthy piece of technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:16.560
uncovered was codenamed “Omega.” Omega&nbsp;
was discovered in an unmarked room on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:22.800
a computer terminal that was connected to&nbsp;
every area of SCP-5001 by dozens of cables.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:28.000
The software itself was an Artificial Intelligence&nbsp;
Construct, a computerized consciousness that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:34.160
seemed to serve the purpose of controlling&nbsp;
the various systems within SCP-5001. The Omega&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:39.360
seemed to work by providing an answer whenever&nbsp;
someone used a keyboard to input a question.&nbsp;

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:44.400
The artificial intelligence of Omega appeared&nbsp;
able to hold a conversation, but would refuse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:50.640
to give any insight into when the SCP-5001&nbsp;
structure was built, or what its purpose was.&nbsp;

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:56.640
Despite neither group knowing what SCP-5001’s&nbsp;
function was, an agreement between the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:02.720
Foundation and GRU Division P was formed. Both&nbsp;
organizations shared the belief that Omega,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:07.520
the Ontological Stabilizers, as well as the&nbsp;
other anomalous technologies could never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:12.080
under any circumstances be allowed&nbsp;
to fall into the wrong hands.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:18.320
They had a pact to keep the knowledge of SCP-5001&nbsp;
and these devices strictly between themselves.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:25.440
However this agreement was, sadly, not to last.
In the early nineties, GRU Division P liquidated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:29.440
its assets and disbanded. A number of&nbsp;
the Russian division’s highest ranking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:34.480
officers stole the anomalous technology that the&nbsp;
organization had in its possession, which they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:40.720
then sold to Marshall, Carter and Dark Ltd.
M, C, and D L-T-D are yet another of the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:45.680
Foundation’s Groups of Interest. According to&nbsp;
Foundation intelligence, Marshall, Carter and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:50.720
Dark Ltd is a London based club that has caused&nbsp;
numerous problems for the Foundation over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:56.480
years. They have ties to wealthy figures across&nbsp;
the globe, and cater to their super rich clientele&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:02.240
by providing them with the most exclusive,&nbsp;
expensive, and rare experiences available.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:08.000
How do they do this? By gathering anomalous items&nbsp;
and auctioning them off to the highest bidders.&nbsp;

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:13.280
A number of GRU Division P operatives also&nbsp;
joined up with The Chaos Insurgency. This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:17.440
a Group of Interest that consists of personnel&nbsp;
who previously worked for the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:22.080
but have since broken away to pursue their&nbsp;
own, rogue agenda. Much like a number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:27.760
other Groups of Interest, the Insurgency uses&nbsp;
anomalies and SCPs for their own benefit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:32.640
as well as dabbling in a bit of arms dealing and&nbsp;
the selling of highly classified intelligence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:37.920
Hey, it’s good to have a diverse portfolio.
Despite former members of GRU Division P&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:43.520
seeking alternative employment with some less&nbsp;
than reputable groups, the SCP Foundation still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:49.840
managed to keep the existence and location of&nbsp;
SCP-5001 a closely guarded secret. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:55.040
even with the structure fully under their control,&nbsp;
their leading researchers were still baffled as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.040 --> 00:11:01.360
to what exactly the purpose of the underground&nbsp;
structure was. Or rather, that was the case.&nbsp;

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:08.560
On December 30th 2019, an explosion erupted in&nbsp;
the northeast sector of SCP-5001, the cause of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:14.240
the explosion was unknown but the damage caused a&nbsp;
tremendous and almost catastrophic loss of power.&nbsp;

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:18.400
Whether the explosion had been triggered by one&nbsp;
of the many Groups of Interest, like the former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:26.320
GRU Division P, or just a machinery malfunction,&nbsp;
it almost caused the total destruction of SC-5001.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:31.360
What would be so bad about that? Well, remember&nbsp;
earlier when we said that every so often an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:36.000
SCP comes along with its very own built in&nbsp;
method of containment? You see, it wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:41.600
the structure or technology of SCP-5001 that&nbsp;
the Foundation should have been worried about:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:49.040
it was the thing inside of SCP-5001.
Just as some Foundation researchers had long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:57.040
theorized, SCP-5001 was a cage, a containment&nbsp;
unit for its own anomalous object within.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.760
Something powerful enough to alter reality&nbsp;
right down to the Humes, hence the need for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:07.680
Ontological Stabilizers to dampen its power and&nbsp;
Omega to keep the place running. This entity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:16.320
known either as SCP-5001-A or “The Devourer”&nbsp;
was being held inside SCP-5001, and when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:23.200
the structure was damaged it was almost freed.
While there was no data on SCP-5001’s computer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:28.400
system about this being’s appearance, or the&nbsp;
extent of its anomalous powers, whoever created&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:34.720
SCP-5001 went to considerable effort to keep The&nbsp;
Devourer contained, viewing it as a threat to all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:40.720
of reality. And all that effort was almost undone&nbsp;
when the structure was damaged by the explosion.&nbsp;

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:46.720
Fortunately, the SCP Foundation was able&nbsp;
to re-establish containment of SCP-5001-A,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:51.120
though at the cost of a tremendous amount of&nbsp;
lives. When personnel were finally permitted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:57.280
to re-enter SCP-5001, a number of the structure’s&nbsp;
core systems had been damaged, but it was still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.280 --> 00:13:02.080
able to perform its primary function and&nbsp;
keep The Devourer safely contained within.&nbsp;

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.880
As personnel entered the&nbsp;
structure, a message appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:09.680
through the Omega computer system that read:
“Hello, my children. Although you have grown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:15.680
immensely since your earliest days, you have&nbsp;
much room to grow. Your species’ intellect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:23.040
is merely a bud, with so much potential. Your&nbsp;
weapons are powerful; your medicine is supreme;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:28.640
your engineering is beautiful. With proper&nbsp;
guidance and care, you are sure to reach an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:34.320
elevated state of being, and transcend your&nbsp;
bodies for something more whole and perfect.&nbsp;

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:40.080
“That is why it pains me so dearly to request that&nbsp;
you leave this place immediately. Your studying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:45.600
and probing have almost resulted in the end of&nbsp;
all I had worked towards to keep you alive. If you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:51.760
comply, I guarantee that The Devourer will never&nbsp;
escape, and your species will be free to pursue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:57.600
the enlightenment of technology for all eternity.
“Let this be my final gift to you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:04.480
directly from the center of my broken heart.”
Okay, back up. “Broken Heart.” Interesting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:09.120
Where have we heard something like that&nbsp;
before? We’d hate to jump to any conclusions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:14.240
but when one hears about a being of great&nbsp;
power, related to large and mysterious machines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:21.520
and that word again - “Broken.” All the groups&nbsp;
of interest that seem to be tied into SCP-5001,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:28.240
and we’d neglected to mention perhaps the most&nbsp;
important of all: The Church of the Broken God.&nbsp;

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:32.800
This religious organization that reveres&nbsp;
industry and technology over the impurity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:39.520
of flesh has been united in a singular purpose:&nbsp;
Rebuilding their deity, the Broken God Mekhane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:44.960
whose body was split apart in an attempt to&nbsp;
preserve the future of mankind. Perhaps the heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:51.840
of this great and ancient machine, this Devourer,&nbsp;
is actually the heart of something else entirely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:56.720
Though of course, there’s only so much we can&nbsp;
speculate. Knowledge, after all, can sometimes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.720 --> 00:15:03.760
be like a flame. It can light your way, but if&nbsp;
you get too close, you will inevitably be burned.&nbsp;

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:09.760
If ever you’re in doubt, ask the people Devoured&nbsp;
and assimilated by the Heart of Mekhane the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:15.840
time it was freed by the Church. If ever the Heart&nbsp;
gets out again, you’ll certainly be with them.&nbsp;

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:23.120
The SCP Foundation has come so far. Their&nbsp;
technology, their knowledge, their vast resources,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:28.640
all allow them to contain some of the most&nbsp;
powerful forces mankind has ever seen, and even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:35.600
some we haven’t. But as SCP-5001 shows, there’s&nbsp;
still much that even the brightest researchers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:41.760
at the Foundation don’t yet understand, and their&nbsp;
drive to poke and prod at the unknown nearly led&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:47.040
to the end of reality as we know it. Perhaps one&nbsp;
day we’ll be able to fully understand just what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:54.000
the Devourer is, and the ways that SCP-5001 worked&nbsp;
to protect us from it, but we’re not there yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:58.640
and there’s no guarantee that we ever will&nbsp;
be. While the pursuit of knowledge is always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:06.160
an admirable one, when it comes to SCP-5001, maybe&nbsp;
the Foundation should have left well enough alone.&nbsp;

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:14.240
Now go check out “SCP-5545 - Mysterious Tunnels&nbsp;
